---
name: evaluate
reasoningEffort: medium
output:
  caseName: string
  fidelity: integer, 0 to 5
  idiomaticity: integer, 0 to 5
  semanticCompression: integer, 0 to 5
  inventedPrimitives: boolean
  missingExpected(array): string
  frictions(array):
    kind: string
    description: string
    likelyKernelGap: boolean
  strongestEvidence: string
---
{{role "system"}}
You evaluate one corpus conversion.

Score fidelity, Arrival idiomaticity, and semantic compression. Do not reward code golf.
Fresh model/agent work should be imported `.prompt` functions; persistent actors should remain
explicit only when their durable hidden state matters.

A valuable `friction` is a semantic requirement that stays awkward despite a good translation.
Set `likelyKernelGap=true` only if it appears to require runtime semantics rather than a library
function or ordinary Scheme composition.

{{role "user"}}
CASE: {{caseName}}

EXPECTED STRESS FEATURES:
{{#each expectedFeatures}}
- {{this}}
{{/each}}

ANALYSIS SUMMARY:
{{compiled.analysis.summary}}

RECOVERED CONTROL FEATURES:
loops={{compiled.analysis.loops}}
branches={{compiled.analysis.branches}}
parallel={{compiled.analysis.parallelRegions}}
actors={{compiled.analysis.persistentActors}}
effects={{compiled.analysis.effects}}
human={{compiled.analysis.humanGates}}
reactive={{compiled.analysis.reactiveConditions}}

LOWERING:
functions={{compiled.lowering.functions}}
prompts={{compiled.lowering.prompts}}
runtimeGaps={{compiled.lowering.runtimeGaps}}

GENERATED PROGRAM:
{{compiled.bundle.program}}

GENERATED PROMPTS:
{{#each compiled.bundle.prompts}}
===== {{path}} =====
{{content}}

{{/each}}

AUDITS:
{{#each compiled.audits}}
- {{lens}}: passed={{passed}}, confidence={{confidence}}
{{/each}}
